* Readme file
/*
This sample race is for a 3-distance 5K, 10K, and Half Marathon using
Race Roster Live Predictive Tracking (LPT).

Participants are separated by the RACE field (5K, 10K, or HALF). Each distance
has its own LPT listing because each course uses different split columns.

Key files:
  - @CalcPlaces       -- Recalculates elapsed times and places.
  - @CalcStatus       -- Refreshes STARTING / IN_PROGRESS / COMPLETE.
  - @ResultsLPTToRR   -- Uploads all three structured LPT result sets.
  - @AutoResultsLPT   -- Combines CalcPlaces + CalcStatus + ResultsLPTToRR.
  - Events2DB         -- Copies start, finish, and split reads to fields.

LPT is structured JSON only. This sample has no unstructured results upload.
Awards still go to a separate unstructured Race Roster result set.

There is deliberately no @AutoResults in this template. Do not mix LPT and
non-LPT uploads on the same Race Roster result set.

Before publishing, seed the dummy Status event with 0 for every bib. Estimated
finish time supplies pace until the runner reaches the first split.

We recommend using Priority and colors to group listing files by function.
*/
